      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## PSL X draft assistant - MANUAL ONLY, DRAFTS ONLY\nSee integrations/n8n/X_DRAFT_ASSISTANT_README.md in the PSL repo.\n1. Config > pslBaseUrl (PSL HTTPS origin, no path). modelId is preconfigured as gpt-4o-mini; maxCompletionTokens 2000 (256-4000).\n2. Header Auth credential **PSL X Drafts** (Authorization: Bearer <X_DRAFT_ASSISTANT_TOKEN>) on the 2 PSL HTTP nodes only. Never the X publisher token.\n3. Header Auth credential **PSL X Draft Model — OpenAI** (Authorization: Bearer <OpenAI project API key>) on the 2 model-call nodes only (attempt 1 and the transient-failure retry).\n4. Use a key from a dedicated, non-default OpenAI project with an ENFORCED monthly hard spend limit. Spend alerts only notify; they do not stop requests. Enforcement is not instantaneous, so spend can slightly exceed the limit.\n5. Keep inactive and manual-only for this pilot. Do not add a Schedule trigger.\n\nPSL's 10-drafts-per-day cap limits SAVED drafts, not model spend. One packet, at most 2 model HTTP attempts (the second only after a timeout, connection error, 408, 5xx, or request/token rate limit; never after authentication, credit, quota, or spend-limit errors), one submission. Refused, truncated, or incomplete output is never submitted. PSL validates the output and saves passing candidates as UNAPPROVED drafts in /admin-social. This workflow cannot approve, schedule, or publish. No X credentials belong here."
      }
    },
